From c56a65b01fbb6e2d61fb91a6f82f9276fc501e1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:56:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: check on the GPU that native Dolby Vision
 frames send the bytes they claim (dvverify)

What native Dolby Vision output does to save GPU time says that it sends the bytes that drawing the
frame plainly sends: a picture that would be drawn again the same way is kept on the screen
(0c1fced); the images of the surfaces of the enhancement layer are kept from one frame to the next
(6d298fb), and a layer whose metadata reconstructs no residual is not imported (0b7b850); the area
around a placed picture is cleared only when it is not black (8dbf285); the bars are written before
the reconstruction, which then skips them, and the planes leave out their rows (Opt1,
libplacebo-9912); a composed picture is packed with one fetch a pixel where fragment shaders have
quad operations (e84aa69); the GPU programs come from the cache of earlier sessions (2ecefa4). The
software bridge measures that; a GPU and its driver are another matter, and nothing checked it there.

<video><dvverify>N</dvverify></video> in advancedsettings.xml checks up to N frames of each native
output. A frame that is checked is drawn a second time, before it is prepared, by a renderer of its
own (dvbridge_render_reference(), dvbridge_verify.c) with all of that off: the picture always
drawn, the layer imported anew whatever its metadata says, the picture black first and the bars
written with the rest, no frame or disabled hook kept from an earlier one, a packer with two fetches,
and its programs compiled from their source (the cache is taken off the GPU while it draws). Its
transport is prepared from the frame's own transport state, at the frame's step-down level and with
its composer (ETSI GS CCM 001 or libplacebo's reshaping), and drawn the way the frame is drawn (the
direct and the composed way differ by a code here and there, by design): what chooses another
picture on purpose is the frame's, what is to send the same bytes is off. After the frame is packed, its transport in the window is copied and compared with the
reference on the GPU, a block of 16x16 pixels for each value of a 240x135 target that is read back
on a later frame, without waiting for it. The log says "dvverify: frame N identical", or how many
pixels differ, in how many blocks, by how many codes, and the first ones with their bytes; and at the
end of the native output how many were identical.

Which refreshes (CDVVerify): the first of each kind of render in the native output (the way, the
residual, the level, bars, drawn or kept: the first use of programs, which may come from the cache),
the first after a change of the level, the first without GUI elements after some with them, the
first that keeps a picture on the screen, and a sample every 100 refreshes. Frames with GUI elements,
overlays or a capture are not checked (what is drawn over the picture is not the reference's). A
refresh that keeps the picture on the screen is checked against the copy of the transport of that
picture, made when it was presented; copies are made only where pictures are kept and a check may
come. A sample waits for a refresh with room, a kept refresh or a frame whose GPU time is at most 3/8
of the refresh (twice that when frames are presented a frame ahead), for 240 refreshes, then is made
anyway: on a GPU without room that can make a frame late. The reference is drawn before the timer of
the frame's GPU work begins, the copy and the comparison after it ends, so that what is measured of
the frame is the frame's; a frame that is checked, and the one after a checked kept refresh, are not
told to the fidelity step-down as presentations. A frame drawn another way than its reference (the
direct way refused it), or without the residual that its reference has (its layer could not be
imported), is not compared, and the check is made at a later refresh.

What it costs while it is in use: a second render, a copy of the 3840x2160 transport and a
comparison for each check; the compile of the reference's programs at its first check of each kind;
a copy for each presented frame where pictures are kept while a check is due; and GPU memory, the
reference's RGBA32F picture (132 MB) and the intermediate textures of its renderer, and two RGBA8
transports (33 MB each). Without the setting nothing of it is made (no renderer, texture, copy or
comparison) and the frames are drawn and presented as before; the only change in the drawing code
is that a renderer can prepare its candidates from another's transport state, which only the
reference does.

Tested on the software bridge (zink on lavapipe) with the profile 7 FEL stream, the frames drawn and
checked as Kodi does it: 20 checks of two pictures (each way, with the stream's bars and without
bars, kept on the screen; composed, placed, placed again, after the GUI drew over the bars, at
another place), all identical, with the renderer's programs taken from the cache of an earlier session and the
reference's compiled (none taken from the cache, none kept in it), with either composer; and the
transport that is presented, frame by frame, the same with the check and without it. Each of these mutations is found
(every check of the mutated case differs, every other one is identical): a picture kept on the
screen across a change of the step-down level (to 3: with the composer of the clause levels 1 and 2
change nothing where the enhancement layer is flat, as it is in the test stream); the GUI drawn over the bars without telling the
renderer; the image of another enhancement surface (the stream's layer is the same picture in every
frame, so the image of an earlier frame would send the same bytes there); a packing with quad
operations that takes a wrong value; and, built from mutated sources, the bars written first a luma
code off (direct) or not quite black (composed), eight rows of the picture left out of the rows that
libplacebo-9912 samples, and the bars of a placed picture taken as clean at any place. CDVVerify has a
host test that each of seven mutations of it fails.

The idea of switches that draw frames again with the optimisations off and compare them on the GPU is
that of the verify switches of the YBLOD fork (DV_VERIFY_*, DV_OVERLAY_INLINE_VERIFY).
